@NAMTIP WONGSOMBOON technical enabler in module P2 Integration, not an application feature. There is no Jira issue {{TE-002}}; use {{RWB-TE-002}} under {{EPIC-001}}. The Feature block quoted is the story’s own §7 Gherkin, and {{Feature: None}} in the story header is correct — it traces to {{REQ-DRI-006}} (BRD Program §7), depends on {{RWB-TE-001}}, and has no screen, API, database object or migration.

It delivers three repository controls: {{.github/CODEOWNERS}}; the {{CodeOwnersValidation}} pull-request pipeline step; and the {{main}} branch rule (require code-owner review, 1 approval, dismiss stale approvals, author’s own approval excluded). Ownership: recovery back end, test, migration and front-end folders plus {{architecture/recovery-modules.yaml}} → {{@scb-ace/techx-recovery-tech-leads}}; common module → {{@scb-ace/ace-team}}; the CODEOWNERS file itself → both teams. Team handles only, never individuals; handles are assumed until DL37/DL36 are answered.

The seven ACs are verification criteria for those repository controls (TC-TE-002-01…08), not business acceptance criteria. Out of scope: the RWB-TE-001 boundary test, collection-module ownership, and the browser test runner (RWB-TE-010). Status in the v2 baseline is {{INC-004}}, “Ready for specify”, with spec/compliance/plan not yet run; the story file v7 header still reads “Ready for build”, and the current baseline carries the 7 ACs.

@SAHIL MORE Follow-up on the synthetic prefix "SYN-" (TE-011 BR3), together with RWB-E1-065:

*Q1. Which fields does "SYN-" apply to?* A prefix works for free-text personal fields (name, address, summary). It cannot be applied to fields with a fixed format: a 13-digit national ID, a phone number, a numeric account number, a date of birth or an amount. Is BR3 meant for free-text fields only?

*Q2. How should fixed-format personal fields be made synthetic?* For example:

* national ID: a deliberately invalid check digit, or a number range that is never issued;
* email: example domains only (e.g. example.com);
* phone: a reserved test range.

Can these rules be added to TE-011 next to BR3, so that the lint and the test data follow one rule?

*Q3. Conflict with RWB-E1-065.* The sandbox generator creates national IDs with a valid check digit (confirmed on TB0001-1226). Those values cannot carry "SYN-", so they fail BR3, and with a valid check digit they also fail BR4. They may also match a real person's ID. Should E1-065 switch to an invalid check digit or an unissued range?

*Q4. Owner.* Please confirm who decides Q1–Q3. Is it the SCB tech lead with the owner of RWB-E1-065, with Privacy consulted?

